<!--Post: 10002--><!--Time: 1109721769-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10002"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 4:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe I&#39;ve missed the answer, but I&#39;ve wondered about this for a while now.  Rocky? Maybe you know?  Both of these women were abducted and found quite a while later.  Any indication if they were killed the same day they were abducted? Why so long before they were found? Did he keep the bodies somewhere else or were they just not discovered?   <BR> <BR>My heart breaks for the victims and their families.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10002-->
<!--Post: 10031--><!--Time: 1109730733-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10031"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 6:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Go to the thread on Victims, you can read about them both, and they were both killed after eating in the same restaurant in Park City, and no not at the same time. E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10031-->
<!--Post: 10036--><!--Time: 1109731906-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10036"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 6:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks but I either miswrote my question or you misread it.  I am completely familiar with the details of the crimes themselves.  My questions was whether there was an indication if each was killed on the day they were abducted and taken to the site where they were found onthe same day and not found until later or left later.  <BR> <BR>It just seems like a long time before the bodies were found. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10036-->
<!--Post: 10047--><!--Time: 1109735835-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10047"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dsv<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dsv<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 7:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another unanswered detail is how he to returned either to work or his home after he dropped the victims bodies and their car in locations far removed from his home or work. <BR> <BR>The drop sites are miles &#40;10 or more&#41; away from his home. I doubt he walked, I guess it&#39;s possible he called a taxi. <BR> <BR>Beatty, the attorney who is writing a book on BTK, suggested on L King that he might have had an accomplice. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10047-->
<!--Post: 10048--><!--Time: 1109735862-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10048"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 7:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I understand what H is asking? I had to read it twice myself. This is very hard, and there is info about that crime scene that could go either way! I won&#39;t elaborate! But if the WPD, feels one way - Marine and Mrs. Davis&#39; cases will also involve kidnapping. Sorry H, I would really love to add what I believe but I won&#39;t because it would involve details. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10048-->
<!--Post: 10049--><!--Time: 1109735928-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10049"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 7:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dsv - I posted that same question under Marine&#39;s folder. Rocky<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10049-->
<!--Post: 10060--><!--Time: 1109737524-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10060"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 8:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, <BR> <BR>I understand completely. Thanks for responding though. There are so many unanswered questions we all have - and I have to believe we may never get answers to some. <BR> <BR>This is so hard for all of you that knew the victims.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10060-->
<!--Post: 10346--><!--Time: 1109904203-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10346"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 6:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>But if the WPD, feels one way - Marine and Mrs. Davis&#39; cases will also involve kidnapping.</i> <BR> <BR>So true, Rocky. At this point, it seems a death penalty won&#39;t be sought. Kidnapping is automatically a Federal crime, making these crimes triable as such, and thus death penalty eligible. But indications are that this won&#39;t happen. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10346-->
<!--Post: 10918--><!--Time: 1110300793-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10918"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 8:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George - why do they keep using the word abducted with Marine and Mrs. Davis then? Wouldn&#39;t that be a form of kidnapping? I don&#39;t know how any of us couldn&#39;t of heard something! My heart breaks thinkin of that. I just wish over and over again,that somehow we could of done something for Marine. This has always weighed very heavy on my  families heart.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10918-->
<!--Post: 11022--><!--Time: 1110359333-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11022"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 1:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So true, Rocky. If a lawyer sees this, please correct me; abduction is kidnapping, yes. And that means FBI. But the FBI is in the case anyway, and I think of that press conference. At the conference, it was dryly explained that no death penalty could be sought as the time frame won&#39;t allow it. I think that WPD, FBI and KBI decided that, no mattter what, Rader would be charged with the ten -- even if he committed others -- who were named and keep it pretty much WPD&#39;s case. <BR> <BR>Pretty sure the FBI can defer to local agencies and apparently this is what happened. The FBI, I believe, could have charged Rader with kidnapping and murdering Ms. Hedge and Mrs. Davis if they had really wanted to, and of course that would have made Rader death penalty-eligible. I guess they just decided to keep everything in Kansas. Rader&#39;s age and the cost of two Federal trials was probably a factor in the FBI&#39;s decision. &#40;I think it would require two separate Federal trials, I&#39;m not sure.&#41; Anyway, in each of these ladies case, the abductions consitute kidnapping. <BR> <BR>I do remember reading something a long time ago about a demand, ransom; there had to be a demand of something by the abductor in order for the crime to &#34;qualify&#34; as kidnapping but I&#39;m not too sure if that is the actual case. There must be a lawyer who reads these boards and who could clear things up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11022-->
</table></td></tr></table>
